Research Writing
================

The `research-writing` skill (skills/research-writing/) combines four
open-source sources. The combined skill is distributed under CC BY-NC 4.0
(see LICENSE), because it includes adapted ARS material. The other skills
in skills/ are separate Nature Skills components and keep their own
Apache-2.0 or MIT licenses (section 3). Each component
below keeps its own license and notices, reproduced in licenses/ or in the
component's directory.

Modifications. Material from every source has been rearranged into the
role structure derived from Paper Orchestra (orchestrate, outline, literature, figures,
draft, review). File locations, cross-references, metadata and hand-off
fields have changed. Runtime adapters, evaluation suites, tests, release
tooling and several optional features have been removed. The router,
role files and the mode files for ARS-derived modes are newly written in
Chinese. In ARS material, product names, paths, version and issue
annotations were rewritten or removed, contract-specific sections were moved
into strict-mode files, environment variables were renamed from ARS_* to
RW_*, and only the scripts the retained documents use were kept. Nature
Skills and K-Dense mode files keep their upstream text apart from renamed
cross-references and paths. SOURCES.md in the repository lists the pinned
upstream revisions and the changes.

